d and a WebGL-capable browser are recommended.",[391],{"_66":392,"_33":393,"_111":-7},"Follow the creator’s complete workflow","https://www.top3d.ai/learn/claude-godot-mcp-3d-game",[395,396,397,398],"Play the web build and study territory capture, trail hazards, enemy movement, and sector progression.","Follow the creator’s tutorial from prototype through materials, audio, effects, and web export.","Read CLAUDE.md to understand the agent, Godot MCP, Blender review, and asset-generation workflow.","Open game/project.godot in Godot 4.7 and press F5; study the scripts alongside the included models, textures, and audio.","The creator documents Claude writing gameplay, shaders, VFX, and UI while a human steers mechanics and materials. The repository includes the actual Godot game, generated assets, and the asset-generation scripts.","3D","Asset creation tools",false,[405,406,407,408,409,410],"assetTools","Blender","Nano Banana","PATINA","Tripo","Stable Audio","ElevenLabs","Godot 4.7 · GDScript",[405,406,407,408,409,410],"3d",[395,396,397,398],{"_66":392,"_33":393,"_25":134},{"_66":388,"_33":365,"_25":308,"_111":389},{"_66":383,"_33":384,"_173":174,"_111":385},{"_66":378,"_33":379,"_111":380},[171,172,420,421],"godot-mcp","mcp-for-blender","example:claude-dreaming-godot","claude-dreaming-godot","Claude Dreaming","Walk from a pixel-art attic into playable 3D paintings: a dream garden, space flight, small planets, and community-built rooms.","/examples/claude-dreaming-godot/",{"_27":423,"_29":424,"_31":425,"_161":411,"_157":413,"_153":164,"_149":482,"_9":483,"_134":484,"_123":485,"_40":486,"_107":487,"_98":488},[429,430,431,432,433,434,435,436,437,438,439,440,441,442,443,444,445,446,447,448],{"_62":29,"_75":424,"_64":29,"_99":-7},{"_62":162,"_75":425,"_64":31,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":159,"_75":411,"_64":161,"_99":150},{"_62":72,"_66":155,"_75":400,"_64":157,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":151,"_75":152,"_64":153,"_99":154},{"_62":72,"_66":147,"_75":482,"_64":149,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":140,"_141":142,"_68":477,"_64":9,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":135,"_68":473,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":132,"_75":134,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":130,"_75":472,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":124,"_68":468,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":121,"_75":308,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":115,"_68":464,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":113,"_75":114,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":105,"_68":460,"_64":107,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":96,"_68":458,"_64":98,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_64":92,"_66":93,"_68":457},{"_62":77,"_64":78,"_66":453,"_80":454,"_82":455,"_40":456,"_85":86,"_87":88,"_89":90},{"_62":72,"_64":73,"_66":74,"_75":452},{"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67,"_68":449},[450],{"_66":67,"_33":451},"https://img.itch.zone/aW1hZ2UvNTExNzQwMi8zMDYzNzA4OS5qcGc=/original/qSShCX.jpg","2026-10-20","Creator-published gameplay screenshot from the itch.io page. The film-derived robot design retains the project-only restrictions recorded in the creator’s NOTICE.md.","/GameMap/media/learning/claude-dreaming-godot.webp","Claude Dreaming gameplay showing a robot floating near a small planet in purple space.","https://rusty-production.itch.io/claude-dreaming",[286],[459],{"_66":102,"_33":103},[461],{"_66":462,"_33":456,"_111":463},"Read the creator’s AI contribution disclosure","The creator explicitly credits Claude and discloses assisted code, graphics, sounds, and text. This is an author disclosure and contribution workflow, not a complete development transcript.",[465],{"_66":298,"_33":466,"_111":467},"https://github.com/moritzfh/claude-dreaming","Full scenes, GDScript, levels, rooms, assets, film intro, and export presets. Run with Godot 4.7.2 standard: import project.godot and press F5. Code is MIT; original assets are CC BY 4.0, while film material and film-derived art have project-only restrictions in NOTICE.md.",[469],{"_66":470,"_33":456,"_111":471},"Play Claude Dreaming","In-development HTML5 game. WASD moves; mouse looks, Space jumps/glides, E enters paintings, R respawns, and Esc pauses. Menus are German; Claude speaks English. The film intro can be skipped.","itch.io",[474],{"_66":475,"_33":476,"_111":-7},"Read how to add a dream with Claude","https://github.com/moritzfh/claude-dreaming/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md",[478,479,480,481],"Start the browser build; hold Enter to skip the film if desired.","Enter a painting and compare its movement with the attic and community rooms.","Import the full project in Godot 4.7.2 standard, then read the level template and contribution guide.","Create one small level through the published API and test entry, movement, respawn, and returning to the attic.","Rusty credits the game to Rusty and Claude and discloses AI assistance for code, graphics, sounds, and text. The repository provides contribution instructions and a level API for building further dreams with Claude.",[478,479,480,481],{"_66":475,"_33":476,"_25":134},{"_66":470,"_33":456,"_25":308,"_111":471},{"_66":298,"_33":466,"_173":174,"_111":467},{"_66":462,"_33":456,"_111":463},[172],"example:deep-yellow-claude","deep-yellow-claude","DEEP YELLOW","Explore procedural Backrooms in a first-person, turn-based roguelike. Moving or waiting triggers combat, while equipment combinations and sanity shape each run.","/examples/deep-yellow-claude/",{"_27":490,"_29":491,"_31":492,"_161":324,"_157":413,"_153":164,"_149":553,"_9":554,"_134":555,"_123":556,"_40":557,"_107":558,"_98":559,"_303":560},[496,497,498,499,500,501,502,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,511,512,513,514,515,516],{"_62":29,"_75":491,"_64":29,"_99":-7},{"_62":162,"_75":492,"_64":31,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":159,"_75":324,"_64":161,"_99":150},{"_62":72,"_66":155,"_75":400,"_64":157,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":151,"_75":152,"_64":153,"_99":154},{"_62":72,"_66":147,"_75":553,"_64":149,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":140,"_141":142,"_68":548,"_64":9,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":135,"_68":545,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":132,"_75":133,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":130,"_75":472,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":124,"_68":541,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":121,"_75":308,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":301,"_68":537,"_64":303,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":115,"_68":533,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":113,"_75":114,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":105,"_68":528,"_64":107,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":96,"_68":525,"_64":98,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_64":92,"_66":93,"_68":524},{"_62":77,"_64":78,"_66":520,"_80":521,"_82":522,"_40":523,"_85":86,"_87":88,"_89":90},{"_62":72,"_64":73,"_66":74,"_75":452},{"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67,"_68":517},[518],{"_66":67,"_33":519},"https://img.itch.zone/aW1hZ2UvNDA2ODk3Ni8yNTU4NTg5NS5wbmc=/original/HZA7lO.png","The author’s Godot play-mode screenshot, retaining the original editor and debug panels.","/GameMap/media/learning/deep-yellow-claude.webp","A first-person yellow-corridor encounter with a held bat, inventory and minimap, inside the creator’s captured Godot editor.","https://aebrer.itch.io/deep-yellow",[95],[526,527],{"_66":102,"_33":103},{"_66":95,"_33":104},[529],{"_66":530,"_33":531,"_111":532},"Read the explicit Claude Code credit","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/blob/master/CREDITS.md#code-and-design","Creator attribution specifically names Claude via Claude Code. The itch page separately discloses AI assistance for code; no complete session transcript is supplied.",[534],{"_66":224,"_33":535,"_111":536},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow","Full Godot 4.6 project, scenes, scripts, assets, shaders, and export presets. The itch page lists code MIT and assets CC0, while CREDITS.md still leaves the original-code license undecided and some third-party licenses unspecified; inspect both before reuse.",[538],{"_66":131,"_33":539,"_111":540},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/releases/tag/v0.13.0","Download — Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.",[542],{"_66":543,"_33":523,"_111":544},"Play DEEP YELLOW","In-development browser build plus Windows/Linux downloads. The creator recommends Chrome or a controller; Firefox mouse input has known problems. Includes horror themes and an interactive tutorial.",[546],{"_66":547,"_33":523,"_111":-7},"Read the creator’s game and development notes",[549,550,551,552],"Play the interactive tutorial and compare moving, waiting, equipment, and sanity.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the project’s separate attribution file.","Import project.godot in Godot 4.6 and inspect the start menu, procedural levels, and turn systems.","Change one equipment or turn rule, then test a complete run and restart.","Drew Brereton identifies the game as code-assisted by Claude. The project credits specifically name Claude Code and distinguish original work from external shaders, textures, and fonts.",[549,550,551,552],{"_66":547,"_33":523,"_25":175},{"_66":543,"_33":523,"_25":308,"_111":544},{"_66":224,"_33":535,"_173":174,"_111":536},{"_66":530,"_33":531,"_111":532},[172,171],[561],{"_333":131,"_33":539,"_25":122,"_111":562},"Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","example:polar-icecapade-claude","polar-icecapade-claude","Polar Icecapade","Slide across icy 3D arenas, use a three-hit melee combo to propel yourself forward, and fire projectiles that push you backward. Open gates and collect coins while confronting a rat regime in a short game-jam adventure.","/examples/polar-icecapade-claude/",{"_27":564,"_29":565,"_31":566,"_161":624,"_157":413,"_153":164,"_149":620,"_404":625,"_9":626,"_134":627,"_123":628,"_40":629,"_107":630,"_98":631},[570,571,572,573,574,575,576,577,578,579,580,581,582,583,584,585,586,587,588,589],{"_62":29,"_75":565,"_64":29,"_99":-7},{"_62":162,"_75":566,"_64":31,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":159,"_75":624,"_64":161,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":401,"_141":402,"_68":621,"_64":404,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":155,"_75":400,"_64":157,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":151,"_75":152,"_64":153,"_99":154},{"_62":72,"_66":147,"_75":620,"_64":149,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":140,"_141":142,"_68":615,"_64":9,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":135,"_68":612,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":132,"_75":133,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":130,"_75":472,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":124,"_68":608,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":121,"_75":308,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":115,"_68":604,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":113,"_75":114,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":105,"_68":600,"_64":107,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":96,"_68":595,"_64":98,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_64":92,"_66":93,"_68":594},{"_62":77,"_64":78,"_66":590,"_80":591,"_82":592,"_40":593,"_85":86,"_87":88,"_89":283},{"_62":72,"_64":277,"_66":278,"_75":452},"The live first level after melee movement and a shot; ammo has fallen to 11/12.","/GameMap/media/learning/polar-icecapade-claude.webp","Polar Icecapade’s first icy 3D arena after melee propulsion and a shot, showing the moving character, gates, coins, timer and 11 of 12 ammunition.","https://evankurtzart.itch.io/polar-icecapade",[95],[596,597,598],{"_66":95,"_33":104},{"_66":102,"_33":103},{"_66":405,"_33":599},"/resources/blender/",[601],{"_66":602,"_33":593,"_111":603},"Read the team’s explicit Claude Code assistance statement","The creators distinguish AI help with diagnosing and implementing core code from their own code review, modeling, animation and art. The page links the full game source and identifies Godot 4.6 and GDScript; its “No generative AI” content badge does not erase the separate coding-assistance disclosure.",[605],{"_66":383,"_33":606,"_111":607},"https://github.com/afenkurtz/Big-Mode-Game-Jam-2026/tree/main/slick","Complete Godot 4.6 project with levels, GDScript, GLB/FBX models, Blender authoring files, textures, UI and audio. The inspected tree has 292 files, about 239 MB. Open the slick folder; importing Blender authoring files may require a compatible Blender installation. No top-level game license was found; external sounds, music and fonts retain their separately credited terms.",[609],{"_66":610,"_33":593,"_111":611},"Play or download Polar Icecapade on itch.io","Mouse recommended: left-click performs melee propulsion, right-click shoots with recoil, and Escape pauses. Browser review reached the first level, moved, fired a projectile with ammo changing from 12 to 11, and opened pause. The roughly 170 MB web build has author-documented performance limits; Windows/Linux downloads are provided and mobile is not recommended. Later levels and a complete run were not tested.",[613],{"_66":614,"_33":593,"_111":-7},"Read the team’s development and asset breakdown",[616,617,618,619],"Start the first browser level with a mouse and test the slippery movement and melee combo.","Use right-click shooting and compare its backward recoil with forward melee propulsion.","Read the team’s Claude Code disclosure and human art, animation and audio credits.","Open the slick project folder in Godot 4.6, change one movement or gate rule, and test the first room, ammo and pause/restart controls.","Aidan “Botodo” Connolly and Evan Kurtz describe Claude Code helping diagnose problems and implement difficult core logic; they then touched and tweaked all code. They modeled, rigged, animated and designed the game themselves, using credited external audio. They explicitly state that generative AI was not used to create assets. No coding model version is supplied.",[405,622,623],"Procreate","Affinity","Godot 4.6 · GDScript · 3D",[405,622,623],[616,617,618,619],{"_66":614,"_33":593,"_25":175},{"_66":610,"_33":593,"_25":308,"_111":611},{"_66":383,"_33":606,"_173":174,"_111":607},{"_66":602,"_33":593,"_111":603},[171,172,632],"blender","example:katana-kitsune-godot","katana-kitsune-godot","Katana Kitsune: Prototype","Choose a kitsune fighter and face yokai in an isometric action roguelike with katana combat, stamina, pickups and successive dungeon floors. The silent prototype supports local multiplayer, with additional party systems documented in the current source.","/examples/katana-kitsune-godot/",{"_27":634,"_29":635,"_31":636,"_161":708,"_157":163,"_153":164,"_149":702,"_404":709,"_9":710,"_134":711,"_123":712,"_40":713,"_107":714,"_98":715},[640,641,642,643,644,645,646,647,648,649,650,651,652,653,654,655,656,657,658,659,660],{"_62":29,"_75":635,"_64":29,"_99":-7},{"_62":162,"_75":636,"_64":31,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":159,"_75":708,"_64":161,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":401,"_141":402,"_68":703,"_64":404,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":155,"_75":156,"_64":157,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":151,"_75":152,"_64":153,"_99":154},{"_62":72,"_66":147,"_75":702,"_64":149,"_99":150},{"_62":91,"_66":140,"_141":142,"_68":697,"_64":9,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":135,"_68":693,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":132,"_75":133,"_64":134,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":130,"_75":472,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":124,"_68":689,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":121,"_75":308,"_64":123,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":115,"_68":685,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":113,"_75":114,"_64":40,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":105,"_68":680,"_64":107,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":96,"_68":670,"_64":98,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_64":92,"_66":93,"_68":668},{"_62":77,"_64":78,"_66":664,"_80":665,"_82":666,"_40":667,"_85":86,"_87":88,"_89":90},{"_62":72,"_64":73,"_66":74,"_75":452},{"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67,"_68":661},[662],{"_66":67,"_33":663},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png","Creator-published combat screenshot from the silent Godot prototype.","/GameMap/media/learning/katana-kitsune-godot.webp","The creator’s Katana Kitsune combat screenshot with an isometric courtyard, the party, enemies, health bars and minimap.","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/blob/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png",[95,669],"GitHub Copilot",[671,672,673,674,675],{"_66":95,"_33":104},{"_66":102,"_33":103},{"_66":678,"_33":679},{"_66":676,"_33":677},{"_66":405,"_33":599},"Meshy API","/resources/meshy/","PixelLab AI Agent Toolkit","/resources/pixellab/",[681],{"_66":682,"_33":683,"_111":684},"Read the creator’s AI production disclosure","https://9-k9.itch.io/katanakitsune","The author explicitly names Claude Code and GitHub Copilot alongside image, sprite and 3D asset tools, and links the primary complete source repository. The README verifies the Godot version and explains which finished assets are included.",[686],{"_66":383,"_33":687,"_111":688},"https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune","Godot 4.7 project with scenes, GDScript, Dialogic addon and finished sprite assets. The inspected tree contains about 383 MB of files; no top-level game license was found. The upstream Meshy/Blender/PixelOver authoring pipeline is separate, while its finished runtime sprites are committed. The current source contains newer party/asset changes than the reviewed hosted prototype.",[690],{"_66":691,"_33":683,"_111":692},"Play Katana Kitsune on itch.io","Silent HTML5 prototype with keyboard and gamepad support. Space confirms player/device choices; allow a clear press and release between setup steps. The browser build loaded and reached player/device selection in review; combat and a complete dungeon run were not exercised. The download is large: about 184 MB of game data plus 40 MB of WebAssembly.",[694],{"_66":695,"_33":696,"_111":-7},"Read the game and asset-pipeline documentation","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune#readme",[698,699,700,701],"Open the itch prototype and choose one human player, then claim a keyboard and select a costume.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the repository’s character, combat and sprite-pipeline notes.","Open project.godot in Godot 4.7 using GL Compatibility; the finished sprites and game scenes are included.","Change one combat or spawn setting, then check the title-to-character-to-dungeon flow, damage and restart.","The creator identifies Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, GPT Image 2, PixelLab and Meshy among the production tools. The repository documents Meshy rigs and animation, Blender retargeting and PixelOver sprite exports. The exact coding models and division of code between assistants are not specified; generated NPC teammates are not the evidence for AI-assisted development.",[704,705,706,405,707],"GPT Image 2","PixelLab","Meshy","PixelOver","Godot 4.7 · GDScript · 2D / GL Compatibility",[704,705,706,405,707],[698,699,700,701],{"_66":695,"_33":696,"_25":175},{"_66":691,"_33":683,"_25":308,"_111":692},{"_66":383,"_33":687,"_173":174,"_111":688},{"_66":682,"_33":683,"_111":684},[171,172,716,717,632],"pixellab","meshy","resource:godot-engine","resource","An open-source 2D and 3D game engine that organizes runnable projects through scenes, nodes, resources, and scripts.","/resources/",{"_27":172,"_787":102,"_153":788,"_62":789,"_786":720,"_781":780,"_33":778,"_63":790,"_763":791,"_754":792,"_751":793,"_748":76},[725,726,727,728,729,730,731,732,733,734,735,736,737],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_62":29,"_75":102,"_64":787,"_99":-7},{"_62":162,"_75":720,"_64":786,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":784,"_75":785,"_64":153,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":782,"_75":783,"_64":62,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_66":779,"_75":780,"_64":781,"_99":150},{"_62":63,"_66":115,"_68":776,"_64":33,"_99":-7},{"_62":63,"_66":769,"_68":770,"_64":63,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_66":761,"_141":402,"_68":762,"_64":763,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_66":752,"_141":402,"_68":753,"_64":754,"_99":-7},{"_62":91,"_66":749,"_141":402,"_68":750,"_64":751,"_99":-7},{"_62":72,"_66":747,"_75":76,"_64":748,"_99":158},{"_62":72,"_64":744,"_66":745,"_75":746},{"_62":63,"_64":738,"_66":739,"_68":740},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[741],{"_66":742,"_33":743},"Godot Engine","htt